    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bd3m",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "ld3j",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "/what-are-common-types-of-product-defects/"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sd3i",
          "text": "Consumers generally have the right to expect that the products they buy and use are safe and will not cause them harm. Unfortunately, some corporations place profits over consumer safety and bring ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sd3k",
          "text": "dangerous, faulty, or toxic",
          "marks": [
            "ld3j"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sd3l",
          "text": " products to market. These decisions can cause serious harm, or even fatal injuries, to unsuspecting consumers.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bd3o",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sd3n",
          "text": "A product liability claim arises when a defect or inherent dangerousness in the design, manufacture, or sale of a product causes injury to a person or persons. Product liability can rest on the designer, manufacturer, or marketer of a product. However, a consumer using a product cannot recover damages if they were using the product for anything other than its proper or intended purpose.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bd3q",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sd3p",
          "text": "Product liability attorneys prove fault by demonstrating a product designer, manufacturer, or marketer of a product:",
          "marks": []
        }
